<title>UK: CE urges Northern to accept offer. [CORRECTED 14:21 GMT]</title>
<headline>CE urges Northern to accept offer. [CORRECTED 14:21 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline to show that CE Electric encouraged shareholders to accept the offer. Earlier Reuters erroneously reported that CE had posted its offer document. This in fact happened on November 5.)</p>
<p>CE Electric, a unit of U.S. group CalEnergy, said on Friday it has posted a letter to Northern Electric Shareholders urging shareholders to accept its offers.  </p>
<p>Energy company CalEnergy is bidding 630p per share for the regional electricity company through its 70 percent owned unit CE Electric and has bought over 29 percent of Northern.</p>
<p>   -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019 (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
